fact WorkItem(id: "WI-1015", description: some(value: "Retire the resolver's Value -> TermId reify; add Value::SymbolRef. `carrier_term` / `reify_goal_value` were the shared 'structural carrier' readers behind the symbol-reflection builtins and field projection. Every remaining use was a READ that TermView answers without allocating, and the reify was not a narrow cost but a WRONG ANSWER on the carriers it declined: `None` for everything but Term/Node (a Value::Entity that plainly has fields; a Value::SymbolRef that IS a symbol), and try_occurrence_to_term's debug_assert!(false) -> Bottom for an Expr::Spliced leaf. MIGRATED: qualified_name, short_name, lookup_symbol, field_name_from_value, resolve_sort_instantiation_param (param symbol AND SortView instance), project_field (now &Value -> Option<Value>, so a Value::Entity receiver projects and the field child keeps its carrier), lower_ho_apply's predicate read plus its sigma chase (walk_view followed a chain only while every link was a Value::Term), and six by-carrier symbol reads outside resolve.rs: value_functor, term_functor_name, dict_resolve_op, view_child_sym, builtin_operation_body, list_items_strict. NEW SEAMS: KnowledgeBase::value_symbol as the one public by-content symbol reader (value_is_unbound_var precedent); finish_result_value so a builtin result binds in the carrier it arrived on; TermPrinter::write_symbol_ref as one owner for the bare-Ref rendering, so two carriers of one symbol cannot key differently in a store key. Value::SymbolRef(Symbol) is the value-level analog of Term::Ref (Value::Var / WI-109 precedent), views as ViewHead::Ref and lowers to Term::Ref; symbol_value in eval/builtins mints it so reflect ops stop interning transients. carrier_term and reify_goal_value are DELETED - the resolver has no Value->TermId reify left. Four tests, each with a MEASURED control. Not driven: the ho_apply sigma-chase widening (needs an initial sigma, which no resolve entry point accepts) - stated at the test site."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-08-05T12:26:42Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-1015", author: "user", content: "CORRECTIONS to this item's own description, from /code-review. (1) FIVE tests, not four. (2) builtin_operation_body is at resolve.rs:4071 — it is NOT one of the 'six by-carrier symbol reads outside resolve.rs'; the five outside are value_functor, term_functor_name, dict_resolve_op, view_child_sym, list_items_strict. (3) The producer flip is REVERTED and moved to WI-1016: minting Value::SymbolRef from symbol_value needs a workspace-wide audit and this item's grep covered only anthill-core/src, so anthill-stl's expect_symbol (5 host ops), MapKey, scalar_eq, detect_cycle, scalar_value_expr, constructor_sub_values, fn_value, is_duplicate_projection and anthill-cli render_value were never scanned. The forced-answer ones are fixed here; the representation decisions are WI-1016. (4) The migration to value_symbol is WIDER than the match it replaced, and a doc comment claimed the opposite: resolve_qualified_name_term deliberately bypasses alloc's nullary-constructor canon, so non-canonicalized Fn{c,[],[]} exist and read as ViewHead::Ref. Doc corrected; the widening is undriven at all five sites. (5) builtin_operation_body and term_functor_name lost their Term::Ident arm to functor_sym, which has none — fixed via a new value_head_symbol, the widest of the three symbol readers. (6) lower_ho_apply hand-rolled a chain walk that this file already owned (SearchStream::walk_value_chain), missing the Value::Var arm and carrying only a 1-cycle guard where a 2-cycle across carriers would HANG; now delegates. (7) ViewItem::to_value bypassed Value::node, the normalizing constructor, so project_field could bind a doubly-wrapped Spliced(Var) that reads as BOUND; fixed at the owner. (8) A regression this item caused on the dot path is recorded as feedback on WI-1014 (occ_head is Opaque for TupleLit/SetLit where the retired reify had real arms). STILL OPEN, not fixed: finish_result_value makes field_access and resolve_sort_instantiation_param into the non-Term extra-binding producers that the WI-649 note at resolve.rs:1102 says do not exist ('safe today only by ABSENCE OF A PRODUCER'), so a projected child sharing a var with the goal binds un-occurs-checked.", at: "2026-08-05T12:15:21Z")
